<title>USA: U.S. factory lard use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory lard use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 33.6 million lbs of lard in edible and inedible product output in December 1996 versus a revised 34.7 million lbs in November and 37.0 million lbs in December 1995, Census Bureau said.</p>
<p>Usage so far in the 1996 period amounted to 415.9 million lbs versus 467.3 million lbs in the 1995 period.</p>
<p>Usage includes hydrogenated vegetable and animal fats and other fats and oils in process.</p>
